<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
    Modem presets card — REBUILT round 9 on the CHANNEL-EDITOR model (owner
    ruling 3). Radio settings → Settings tab. Two sub-tabs:

      "Preset programming"  LEFT, DEFAULT — the preset picker (0-6 at an
                            SSB or ALE prompt, 7-9 at a HOP one — clone-field
                            round 2 F11) with the picked preset's SINGLE LIST
                            ROW beside it (the same projection the list tab
                            renders — two views of one preset cannot
                            disagree), a Name entry, the type-switched
                            selections, the baud wheel, and ONE Store.
      "Preset list"         RIGHT — the stored presets, READ-ONLY: # and
                            Name parsed, Parameters VERBATIM.

    ROUND 9 CHANGES, in one place:
      - The three blue per-field displays (name / baud / interleave) are
        DELETED. The read-back row beside the picker is the ONE value
        display on this card.
      - Value tokens on the wire are the HELP screen's ABBREVIATIONS; the
        buttons show human-readable WORDS (ModemPresetVocabulary owns both
        columns plus the listing spellings that prefill them).
      - The four segment rows (Type / Interleave / Mode / Preset state)
        RIGHT-ALIGN, house 6-dp spacing.

    ROUND 10 (§3/§8), on top of that:
      - PLACEMENT is now per-row (owner-final 2026-08-16): Type, Mode and
        Preset state carry their labels LEFT like every other row in the app;
        INTERLEAVE alone keeps its label ABOVE — the ONE sanctioned above-label
        row, ledger-recorded, because its five buttons need the full card
        width. The round-9 "labels above as a class" is retired, and so is the
        row-local TypeRowSpacing knob: the WIDTHS carry the fit now.
      - The rows SPLIT: Type 3+3 and Interleave 3+2 at SegmentWidthWide (90),
        Mode 2+1 at SegmentWidthXWide (132) with the full port words. The
        row label is "Mode", because the buttons say "port".
        (ROUND 11 §3 supersedes both halves of that line — see below.)
      - The read-back beside the picker is the ENRICHED projection: two fixed
        header+value lines (# | Name | Type | Data mode, then Baud |
        Interleave OR Mark+Space | State), falling back to ONE VERBATIM
        Parameters cell when the mandatory Type/Data-mode/Baud trio does not
        all map. The LIST tab is UNCHANGED — still # | Name | verbatim
        Parameters.
      - Baud is a ◀ display ▶ WHEEL over the discrete HELP set. Its display
        shows the operator's PENDING SELECTION, not radio state — a
        deliberate deviation from the Option-B rule, recorded in ui.md;
        radio state lives on the read-back row.
      - Interleave renders only under 39-tone / Serial (ASSUMED — a
        tone-waveform inference, bench item A6d); Mark/Space only under the
        four FSK types; neither while no type is selected.
        (ROUND 11 §6 supersedes both halves: the interleave inference is now
        VERIFIED and additionally excludes Serial at 4800, and Mark/Space are
        offered at FSK VFT ALONE. The ROW PROJECTION's type map is unchanged —
        see below.)
      - NO Refresh button: every EDITOR LANDING (view Loaded, Ready arrival,
        picker spin, programming-tab landing) sends a fresh MODEM PRE. The
        preset LIST tab is the lazy tier.

    ROUND 11 (§3/§6), on top of that:
      - The "Mode" row is the PORT row: label "Port", buttons "Remote port
        (async)" / "Data port (async)" / "Data port (sync)". The TYPE words
        are "39 tone" / "Serial" / "FSK wide" / "FSK narrow" / "FSK ASCII" /
        "FSK VFT". Display text only — every wire token is untouched.
      - Both rows move to SegmentWidthPort, where the budget is TWO
        buttons per line: Type is 2+2+2 (replacing round 10's 3+3 at 90) and
        Port is 2+1. Interleave and Preset state stay at SegmentWidthWide.
        (CLONE ROUND 12 §9 A5: that shared width goes 136 -> 184 on the owner's
        ruling — 136 CLIPPED "Remote port (async)" and the 336-dp phone budget
        that blocked widening was itself stale. See App.xaml.)
      - The READ MODEL has two sources (§6). The LIST tab's once-per-session
        landing runs the seven-preset FIELD batch and then queues the bulk
        PRESENCE read behind it; the §8 single-slot modem queue is what makes
        that order real, and it is why a targeted row can never be counted as
        "enabled". The EDITOR reads ONE preset targeted per landing/spin.
      - The list gains a STATE column: "Enabled" iff a COMPLETED presence read
        listed the preset, "Disabled" iff it did not, "—" while unknown or in
        flight.

    CLONE ROUND 12 §9 A3, on top of that:
      - The READ-BACK block beside the picker binds PRESENCE too. Round 11 left
        its "State" cell on the listing-derived value, which no capture has
        ever carried — structurally always "—", so the operator programming a
        preset was the one person who could not see whether the write took. The
        listing-derived cell is DELETED from the projection.
      - PRESENCE is therefore whole-card: it runs ONCE per session behind its
        own gate, on whichever tab lands first, separate from the list tab's
        seven-read field batch.
      - The offers are TYPE-SCOPED (§6): the baud wheel cycles only what the
        picked type stores (every excess is silently CLAMPED), interleave
        offers 39-tone LO/SH/ALTS/ALTL and Serial LO/SH/ZE below 4800 and
        hides otherwise, and MARK/SPACE (350-3250) appear at FSK VFT only.
      - An INTERLEAV-carrying write is REFUSED app-side at an ALE> prompt: the
        radio swallows it there.

    Wire notes: MODEM PRE is bench-confirmed at SSB/ALE prompts, UNPROBED
    from HOP. The ARGUMENT NAMES of the write are the session-15 form; the
    short VALUE tokens are HELP-derived and their write acceptance is
    ASSUMED (bench item A6d). The programming ECHO is a listing-form line and
    upserts the mirror — but it cannot show a clamp or a state change, so
    round 11 re-reads the written preset targeted, plus the presence read when
    the line carried EN/DIS.

    Gate: Ready AND a CONFIRMED MODE (clone-field round 2 F11). The card sits
    on the mode-free Radio settings page — the radio-clock precedent, which is
    why the gate was Ready ALONE until F11 — but the card's SHAPE is now a
    claim about which presets the radio has, and that is a fact about the
    PROMPT. Unconfirmed: every control dark with its reason, no read, no Store.
    BindingContext = ModemPresetsViewModel (DI singleton,
    code-behind — the DeviceClockView pattern); Loaded fires the landing read.
-->
<ContentView xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             xmlns:vm="clr-namespace:Falcon.App.Core.ViewModels;assembly=Falcon.App.Core"
             xmlns:behaviors="clr-namespace:Falcon.App.Behaviors"
             x:Class="Falcon.App.Views.SettingsParts.ModemPresetsView"
             x:DataType="vm:ModemPresetsViewModel">
    <ContentView.Resources>
        <!-- The row cell widths, shared by the read-back block and the list
             tab so the two renderings of one preset line up (rule K). -->
        <x:Double x:Key="PresetWidthNumber">28</x:Double>
        <x:Double x:Key="PresetWidthName">56</x:Double>
        <!-- Round 10 §8: the enriched read-back's field cells (Type, Baud,
             Interleave / Mark / Space), sized to their widest display word
             ("39-tone", "Alt short", six mark digits). -->
        <x:Double x:Key="PresetWidthField">76</x:Double>

        <!-- ROUND 10 §3: the choice buttons are the WIDE classes now, so the
             round-9 row-local TypeRowSpacing knob is gone — every row uses the
             house 6 dp and the WIDTHS carry the fit (StyleVocabularyGuardTests
             owns the arithmetic).

             Two templates, one per width class: SegmentWidthWide (90) for
             interleave / preset state, and — ROUND 11 §3 — SegmentWidthPort
             for the TYPE and PORT rows, whose words are the card's longest
             ("Remote port (async)", "FSK narrow"). ONE key drives both rows,
             which is why clone round 12 §9 A5 widened them TOGETHER, exactly
             as the owner's ruling asked. -->
        <DataTemplate x:Key="PresetChoiceButton" x:DataType="vm:ChoiceItem">
            <Button Text="{Binding Value}" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                    WidthRequest="{StaticResource SegmentWidthWide}"
                    Command="{Binding SelectCommand}"
                    SemanticProperties.Description="{Binding Value}">
                <Button.Triggers>
                    <DataTrigger TargetType="Button" Binding="{Binding IsActive}" Value="True">
                        <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="{StaticResource AccentColor}" />
                        <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="{StaticResource OnAccentColor}" />
                    </DataTrigger>
                </Button.Triggers>
            </Button>
        </DataTemplate>

        <DataTemplate x:Key="PresetPortChoiceButton" x:DataType="vm:ChoiceItem">
            <Button Text="{Binding Value}" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                    WidthRequest="{StaticResource SegmentWidthPort}"
                    Command="{Binding SelectCommand}"
                    SemanticProperties.Description="{Binding Value}">
                <Button.Triggers>
                    <DataTrigger TargetType="Button" Binding="{Binding IsActive}" Value="True">
                        <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="{StaticResource AccentColor}" />
                        <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="{StaticResource OnAccentColor}" />
                    </DataTrigger>
                </Button.Triggers>
            </Button>
        </DataTemplate>
    </ContentView.Resources>

    <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}">
        <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10">

            <Label Text="Modem presets" Style="{StaticResource CardHeading}" />

            <Label Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="{Binding DisabledReason}"
                   IsVisible="{Binding HasDisabledReason}" />

            <!-- Sub-tab strip: pure view state. Landing on programming
                 re-reads (an editor landing); landing on the list reads only
                 if nothing has loaded it yet this session. -->
            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,*" ColumnSpacing="6">
                <Button Text="Preset programming" Style="{StaticResource Segment}" HorizontalOptions="Fill"
                        Command="{Binding OpenProgrammingTabCommand}"
                        SemanticProperties.Description="Preset programming tab (picker and editor)">
                    <Button.Triggers>
                        <DataTrigger TargetType="Button" Binding="{Binding IsListTabOpen}" Value="False">
                            <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="{StaticResource AccentColor}" />
                            <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="{StaticResource OnAccentColor}" />
                        </DataTrigger>
                    </Button.Triggers>
                </Button>
                <Button Grid.Column="1" Text="Preset list" Style="{StaticResource Segment}" HorizontalOptions="Fill"
                        Command="{Binding OpenListTabCommand}"
                        SemanticProperties.Description="Preset list tab (stored presets, read-only)">
                    <Button.Triggers>
                        <DataTrigger TargetType="Button" Binding="{Binding IsListTabOpen}" Value="True">
                            <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="{StaticResource AccentColor}" />
                            <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="{StaticResource OnAccentColor}" />
                        </DataTrigger>
                    </Button.Triggers>
                </Button>
            </Grid>

            <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10" IsEnabled="{Binding AreControlsEnabled}">

                <!-- ========= Preset programming tab ========= -->
                <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10" IsVisible="True">
                    <VerticalStackLayout.Triggers>
                        <DataTrigger TargetType="VerticalStackLayout" Binding="{Binding IsListTabOpen}" Value="True">
                            <Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="False" />
                        </DataTrigger>
                    </VerticalStackLayout.Triggers>

                    <!-- Picker + read-back (ruling 3, the channel editor's
                         CH/EC shape): the spinner in column 0, the picked
                         preset's SINGLE LIST ROW beside it in the star
                         column, centred there. Every cell renders only from
                         MODEM PRE lines, "—" until one arrives; Parameters
                         wraps under its heading. -->
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="10">
                        <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="0">
                            <Button Text="▲" FontSize="10" Padding="0"
                                    WidthRequest="44" HeightRequest="44"
                                    Command="{Binding PresetUpCommand}"
                                    SemanticProperties.Description="Next preset (re-reads the stored presets)" />
                            <Label Text="{Binding PickedPresetText}" FontSize="30"
                                   FontAttributes="Bold" FontFamily="Consolas"
                                   WidthRequest="44" HorizontalTextAlignment="Center" />
                            <Button Text="▼" FontSize="10" Padding="0"
                                    WidthRequest="44" HeightRequest="44"
                                    Command="{Binding PresetDownCommand}"
                                    SemanticProperties.Description="Previous preset (re-reads the stored presets)" />
                        </VerticalStackLayout>

                        <!-- ROUND 10 §8 — the ENRICHED read-back. TWO fixed
                             header+value grid LINES (the SSB read-back
                             precedent):
                               line 1  #  |  Name  |  Type  |  Data mode
                               line 2  Baud | Interleave OR Mark+Space | State
                             …and Interleave-vs-Mark/Space follows the round-9
                             TYPE MAP, per row.

                             The whole parsed block renders only when the row
                             PARSED — Type + Data mode + Baud all mapped through
                             the vocabulary's listing forms. Anything unmapped in
                             that mandatory trio and the block is replaced by the
                             ONE VERBATIM cell below it: the AGC precedent, no
                             column ever invented. (State is OPTIONAL and shows
                             "—": its listing spellings have never been captured,
                             so an absent state is a normal row.) -->
                        <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Column="1" Spacing="2" VerticalOptions="Center"
                                             HorizontalOptions="Center">
                            <!-- LINE 1: # | Name | Type | Data mode. The # and
                                 Name cells are the round-9 contract and always
                                 render (they are parsed by the listing SHAPE);
                                 the two vocabulary cells beside them belong to
                                 the parsed projection and go with it. -->
                            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="8">
                                <Label Text="#" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                       WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthNumber}" />
                                <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="Name" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                       WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthName}" />
                                <Label Grid.Column="2" Text="Type" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                       WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthField}"
                                       IsVisible="{Binding PickedRow.ShowsType}" />
                                <Label Grid.Column="3" Text="Data mode" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                       IsVisible="{Binding PickedRow.ShowsType}" />
                                <!-- THE HOP SHAPE'S OWN TWO COLUMNS (audit round
                                     1, MAJOR 3). A `HOP>` row has no TYPE field
                                     at all and carries its mode phrase as two
                                     independent words, so it reads back as
                                     Signalling + Port — the same two columns the
                                     editor offers. Exactly one of the two pairs
                                     is ever visible, so they share the cells. -->
                                <Label Grid.Column="2" Text="Signalling" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                       WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthField}"
                                       IsVisible="{Binding PickedRow.IsHopShape}" />
                                <Label Grid.Column="3" Text="Port" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                       IsVisible="{Binding PickedRow.IsHopShape}" />
                            </Grid>
                            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="8">
                                <Label Text="{Binding PickedRow.NumberText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                       WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthNumber}"
                                       SemanticProperties.Description="Picked preset number" />
                                <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding PickedRow.NameText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                       WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthName}"
                                       SemanticProperties.Description="Stored preset name" />
                                <Label Grid.Column="2" Text="{Binding PickedRow.TypeText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                       WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthField}"
                                       IsVisible="{Binding PickedRow.ShowsType}"
                                       SemanticProperties.Description="Reported modem type" />
                                <Label Grid.Column="3" Text="{Binding PickedRow.DataModeText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                       IsVisible="{Binding PickedRow.ShowsType}"
                                       SemanticProperties.Description="Reported data mode" />
                                <Label Grid.Column="2" Text="{Binding PickedRow.SyncText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                       WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthField}"
                                       IsVisible="{Binding PickedRow.IsHopShape}"
                                       SemanticProperties.Description="Reported signalling" />
                                <Label Grid.Column="3" Text="{Binding PickedRow.PortText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                       IsVisible="{Binding PickedRow.IsHopShape}"
                                       SemanticProperties.Description="Reported port" />
                            </Grid>

                            <!-- LINE 2, parsed only. -->
                            <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="2" IsVisible="{Binding PickedRow.IsParsed}">
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="8" Margin="0,4,0,0">
                                    <Label Text="Baud" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                           WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthField}" />
                                    <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="Interleave" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                           WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthField}"
                                           IsVisible="{Binding PickedRow.ShowsInterleave}" />
                                    <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="Mark" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                           WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthField}"
                                           IsVisible="{Binding PickedRow.ShowsMarkSpace}" />
                                    <Label Grid.Column="2" Text="Space" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                           WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthField}"
                                           IsVisible="{Binding PickedRow.ShowsMarkSpace}" />
                                    <Label Grid.Column="3" Text="State" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}" />
                                </Grid>
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="8">
                                    <Label Text="{Binding PickedRow.BaudText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                           WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthField}"
                                           SemanticProperties.Description="Reported baud" />
                                    <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding PickedRow.InterleaveText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                           WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthField}"
                                           IsVisible="{Binding PickedRow.ShowsInterleave}"
                                           SemanticProperties.Description="Reported interleave" />
                                    <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding PickedRow.MarkText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                           WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthField}"
                                           IsVisible="{Binding PickedRow.ShowsMarkSpace}"
                                           SemanticProperties.Description="Reported FSK mark" />
                                    <Label Grid.Column="2" Text="{Binding PickedRow.SpaceText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                           WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthField}"
                                           IsVisible="{Binding PickedRow.ShowsMarkSpace}"
                                           SemanticProperties.Description="Reported FSK space" />
                                    <!-- CLONE ROUND 12 §9 A3: PRESENCE, not the
                                         deleted listing-derived StateText. The
                                         listing never carries a preset's
                                         enabled state, so this cell was
                                         structurally always "—". -->
                                    <Label Grid.Column="3" Text="{Binding PickedRow.PresenceText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                           SemanticProperties.Description="Reported preset state" />
                                </Grid>
                            </VerticalStackLayout>

                            <!-- The FALLBACK: ONE verbatim cell, the radio's own
                                 text, whenever the shape's mandatory set did not
                                 all map (and for a preset the radio has never
                                 listed). It replaces BOTH parsed tails — there
                                 is nothing honest to put in a typed column when
                                 the token that names it is unknown.
                                 A `HOP>` row does NOT come here (audit round 1,
                                 MAJOR 3): its shape is first-class, with the
                                 pair port · baud mandatory instead of the SSB
                                 trio, so it reads back typed like any other. -->
                            <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="2" Margin="0,4,0,0"
                                                 IsVisible="{Binding PickedRow.IsNotParsed}">
                                <Label Text="Parameters" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}" />
                                <Label Text="{Binding PickedRow.ParametersText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                       LineBreakMode="CharacterWrap"
                                       SemanticProperties.Description="Stored preset parameters, verbatim" />
                            </VerticalStackLayout>
                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                    </Grid>

                    <!-- Name: hint placeholder only (K5/X5 — a report never
                         writes this buffer). Empty at Store re-sends the
                         reported name; nothing reported refuses. -->
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="6">
                        <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="Name" />
                        <Entry Grid.Column="1" MaxLength="4"
                               Placeholder="1-4 letters or digits"
                               Text="{Binding NameInput, Mode=TwoWay}"
                               SemanticProperties.Description="Preset name entry — empty re-stores the reported name">
                            <Entry.Behaviors>
                                <behaviors:SelectAllOnFocusBehavior />
                            </Entry.Behaviors>
                        </Entry>
                    </Grid>

                    <!-- ==== THE SSB / ALE FIELD STACK (clone-field round 2
                         F11, owner ruling R-D, decision A-9) ================
                         The card FOLLOWS THE CONFIRMED MODE, and the two shapes
                         are two stacks with exactly one visible. This one is
                         the card as it has always been — Type, Interleave and
                         the welded Port phrase — and it is byte-for-byte
                         unchanged inside. Its HOP twin is below.

                         ABSENT, not greyed: a `HOP>` preset HAS no type,
                         interleave or mark/space field (P5/P5b — a `TYPE`
                         argument draws `** ERROR **` there), so under HOP these
                         rows are not rendered at all. A disabled control would
                         say "not now"; the truth is "not on this radio's hop
                         presets". -->
                    <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10" IsVisible="{Binding IsSsbScope}">

                    <!-- Type — REQUIRED. ROUND 11 §3: label LEFT, THREE ROWS OF
                         TWO at SegmentWidthPort, replacing round 10's 3+3 at
                         SegmentWidthWide. The per-row budget is the gate
                         StyleVocabularyGuardTests evaluates; at §9 A5's widened
                         184 against the corrected 448-dp phone budget that is
                         2×184+6 = 374 ≤ 448−48−6 = 394 for a "Type" label
                         allowance of 48. This is the TIGHTER of the two rows
                         sharing the width, so it is the one that gates it. -->
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="6">
                        <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="Type" />
                        <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Column="1" Spacing="6" HorizontalOptions="End">
                            <HorizontalStackLayout Spacing="6" HorizontalOptions="End"
                                                   BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding TypeChoicesRow1}"
                                                   BindableLayout.ItemTemplate="{StaticResource PresetPortChoiceButton}" />
                            <HorizontalStackLayout Spacing="6" HorizontalOptions="End"
                                                   BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding TypeChoicesRow2}"
                                                   BindableLayout.ItemTemplate="{StaticResource PresetPortChoiceButton}" />
                            <HorizontalStackLayout Spacing="6" HorizontalOptions="End"
                                                   BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding TypeChoicesRow3}"
                                                   BindableLayout.ItemTemplate="{StaticResource PresetPortChoiceButton}" />
                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                    </Grid>

                    <!-- Interleave — OPTIONAL (tap the lit segment to clear =
                         omitted from the line). 39-tone / Serial only
                         (ASSUMED — bench item A6d).
                         ROUND 10 §3: this is the ONE owner-chosen label-ABOVE
                         row in the app (ledger-recorded). Its five buttons need
                         the FULL card width — 3+2 at SegmentWidthWide — and a
                         left label would not leave it. -->
                    <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="6" IsVisible="{Binding ShowInterleave}">
                        <Label Text="Interleave" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" />
                        <HorizontalStackLayout Spacing="6" HorizontalOptions="End"
                                               BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding InterleaveChoicesRow1}"
                                               BindableLayout.ItemTemplate="{StaticResource PresetChoiceButton}" />
                        <HorizontalStackLayout Spacing="6" HorizontalOptions="End"
                                               BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding InterleaveChoicesRow2}"
                                               BindableLayout.ItemTemplate="{StaticResource PresetChoiceButton}" />
                    </VerticalStackLayout>

                    <!-- Port (the data-mode field) — REQUIRED. ROUND 11 §3: the
                         row label is "Port", because the BUTTONS name the port
                         and put the signalling behind it ("Remote port (async)"
                         / "Data port (async)" / "Data port (sync)"), at
                         SegmentWidthPort, 2+1. Label LEFT, allowance 36:
                         2×184+6 = 374 ≤ 448−36−6 = 406 (§9 A5). The VM property is
                         still DataMode* — a display rename never touches an
                         internal name (invariant 4). -->
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="6">
                        <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="Port" />
                        <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Column="1" Spacing="6" HorizontalOptions="End">
                            <HorizontalStackLayout Spacing="6" HorizontalOptions="End"
                                                   BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding DataModeChoicesRow1}"
                                                   BindableLayout.ItemTemplate="{StaticResource PresetPortChoiceButton}" />
                            <HorizontalStackLayout Spacing="6" HorizontalOptions="End"
                                                   BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding DataModeChoicesRow2}"
                                                   BindableLayout.ItemTemplate="{StaticResource PresetPortChoiceButton}" />
                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                    </Grid>

                    </VerticalStackLayout>
                    <!-- ==== end of the SSB / ALE field stack ============== -->

                    <!-- ==== THE HOP FIELD STACK (F11) ====================
                         A `HOP>` preset is name / signalling / port / baud and
                         nothing else, and its mode phrase is TWO INDEPENDENT
                         WORDS on the wire — P5b applied `SYNC DATA` on its own
                         and `ASYNC REMOTE` on its own — so it is two rows here
                         rather than the SSB card's one welded phrase. Both are
                         REQUIRED: the line has no form without them. -->
                    <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10" IsVisible="{Binding IsHopScope}">

                        <!-- Signalling — REQUIRED. Two short words, so the
                             narrower segment template. -->
                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="6">
                            <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="Signalling" />
                            <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Column="1" Spacing="6" HorizontalOptions="End"
                                                   BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding SyncChoices}"
                                                   BindableLayout.ItemTemplate="{StaticResource PresetChoiceButton}" />
                        </Grid>

                        <!-- Port — REQUIRED. The full port words, so the
                             PresetPortChoiceButton width the SSB Port row uses. -->
                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="6">
                            <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="Port" />
                            <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Column="1" Spacing="6" HorizontalOptions="End"
                                                   BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding PortChoices}"
                                                   BindableLayout.ItemTemplate="{StaticResource PresetPortChoiceButton}" />
                        </Grid>

                    </VerticalStackLayout>
                    <!-- ==== end of the HOP field stack ==================== -->

                    <!-- Baud — the ◀ display ▶ wheel over the DISCRETE HELP
                         set (75/150/300/600/1200/2400/4800/Voice, wrapping).
                         SHARED between the two shapes (F11): under a confirmed
                         HOP the same wheel offers the MEASURED hop set
                         {75, 150, 300} instead — P5c swept nine other values
                         and every one was SILENTLY ignored, so offering them
                         would be offering a lie.
                         The display carries the operator's PENDING SELECTION
                         in display words, fixed width (rule K), "—" until
                         prefilled or spun. Chevrons are chevron-class 44 dp. -->
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="6">
                        <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="Baud" />
                        <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Column="1" Spacing="6" HorizontalOptions="End">
                            <Button Text="◀" FontSize="10" Padding="0"
                                    WidthRequest="44" HeightRequest="44"
                                    Command="{Binding BaudDownCommand}"
                                    SemanticProperties.Description="Previous baud" />
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource ValueDisplay}" WidthRequest="72"
                                    SemanticProperties.Description="Baud to be stored">
                                <Label Style="{StaticResource ValueDisplayText}"
                                       Text="{Binding BaudText}" />
                            </Border>
                            <Button Text="▶" FontSize="10" Padding="0"
                                    WidthRequest="44" HeightRequest="44"
                                    Command="{Binding BaudUpCommand}"
                                    SemanticProperties.Description="Next baud" />
                        </HorizontalStackLayout>
                    </Grid>

                    <!-- MARK/SPACE: FSK types only (type-switched). A pair or
                         nothing; units PROVISIONAL. -->
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="6"
                          IsVisible="{Binding ShowMarkSpace}">
                        <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="Mark" />
                        <Entry Grid.Column="1" Keyboard="Numeric"
                               Placeholder="digits (provisional)"
                               Text="{Binding MarkInput, Mode=TwoWay}"
                               SemanticProperties.Description="FSK mark frequency — provisional, units unverified" />
                        <Label Grid.Column="2" VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="Space" />
                        <Entry Grid.Column="3" Keyboard="Numeric"
                               Placeholder="digits (provisional)"
                               Text="{Binding SpaceInput, Mode=TwoWay}"
                               SemanticProperties.Description="FSK space frequency — provisional, units unverified" />
                    </Grid>

                    <!-- Preset state — OPTIONAL (tap the lit segment to
                         clear). Never prefills: no capture has ever echoed a
                         preset's state. ROUND 10 §3: label LEFT, one row of
                         two at SegmentWidthWide. -->
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="6">
                        <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="Preset state" />
                        <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Column="1" Spacing="6" HorizontalOptions="End"
                                               BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding StateChoices}"
                                               BindableLayout.ItemTemplate="{StaticResource PresetChoiceButton}" />
                    </Grid>

                    <!-- ONE Store — the whole preset as one line. The echoed
                         listing line UPSERTS the mirror, but round 11 §6
                         retired "the echo IS the read-back" for this card: it
                         cannot show a silently clamped baud and never carries
                         the enabled state, so the press also re-reads the
                         preset targeted (plus the presence op when the line
                         carried EN/DIS). Round 10 §3: ACTION class —
                         DE-PINNED, natural width. -->
                    <Button Text="Store" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                            HorizontalOptions="End"
                            Command="{Binding StoreCommand}"
                            SemanticProperties.Description="Program this preset on the radio" />

                    <Label Style="{StaticResource ErrorCaption}" Text="{Binding InputError}"
                           IsVisible="{Binding HasInputError}" />
                </VerticalStackLayout>

                <!-- ========= Preset list tab ========= -->
                <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="6" IsVisible="False">
                    <VerticalStackLayout.Triggers>
                        <DataTrigger TargetType="VerticalStackLayout" Binding="{Binding IsListTabOpen}" Value="True">
                            <Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="True" />
                        </DataTrigger>
                    </VerticalStackLayout.Triggers>

                    <!-- ROUND 11 §6: the STATE column. It is the ONLY cell here
                         that does not come from the preset's line — the line
                         never carries the enabled state. It comes from the
                         PRESENCE operation this tab's landing runs behind its
                         field batch, and it renders three states: "Enabled",
                         "Disabled", and "—" while no presence read has
                         completed or one is in flight. -->
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="8">
                        <Label Text="#" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                               WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthNumber}" />
                        <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="Name" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                               WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthName}" />
                        <Label Grid.Column="2" Text="State" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                               WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthField}" />
                        <Label Grid.Column="3" Text="Parameters" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}" />
                    </Grid>

                    <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="6"
                                         BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding Rows}">
                        <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                            <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:ModemPresetRow">
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="8">
                                    <Label Text="{Binding NumberText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                           WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthNumber}"
                                           SemanticProperties.Description="Preset number" />
                                    <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding NameText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                           WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthName}"
                                           SemanticProperties.Description="Stored preset name" />
                                    <Label Grid.Column="2" Text="{Binding PresenceText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                           WidthRequest="{StaticResource PresetWidthField}"
                                           SemanticProperties.Description="Preset enabled state" />
                                    <Label Grid.Column="3" Text="{Binding ParametersText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                           LineBreakMode="CharacterWrap"
                                           SemanticProperties.Description="Stored preset parameters, verbatim" />
                                </Grid>
                            </DataTemplate>
                        </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                    </VerticalStackLayout>

                    <Label Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                           IsVisible="{Binding HasNoPresets}"
                           Text="No presets reported yet." />
                </VerticalStackLayout>
            </VerticalStackLayout>
        </VerticalStackLayout>
    </Border>
</ContentView>
